Z||000003||turbo86se||10-29-1999||11:44 AM||||Thanks a lot DAD, let me know what you come up with. I really appreciate it! My fiero-maniac mechanic does have three parts cars with good Isuzu transmissions available, what do you think about using the Isuzu with the stock V6? I've read somewhere you can use a 6-cylinder clutch in the set up, is that true? Are any certain year's better than the other, as far as transmissions? Two are from '85s, and the other is from a '87.<BR>Thanks again!||||reg||7
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||10-29-1999||01:42 PM||||I have an Isuzu tranny in my 88 coupe to stir the gears for the 2.8 V6 I installed. It is holding up fine after many autocrosses and a few passes down the local dragstrip.<P>I learned the hard way about what clutch to use...I ended up doing it twice. Someone told me to use the V6 clutch inside the Isuzu <B>WRONG!!!</B>||||reg||6
Z||000005||bHooper||10-29-1999||04:10 PM||||SCCA, I may actually be close to buying an Isuzu for my GT.  I found a virgin fiero in a local salvage yard, an '86 4 cyl.  The funny thing is, there may actually be nothing wrong with the car.  They said it had a bad carb....?  The paint is rough and the grey int is perfect (the car has been under trees for the past 6 years)...a perfect donor/parts car to help restore my GT... if I get it for the right price..the car has no title or keys, the hood latch doesnt open...who knows..<BR>Brian||||reg||1
